course: dictionary
lesson: 629
title: Who looks after the children?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A babysitter is a person who looks after children in their home while the parents are out, usually for a few hours and often for money. The clues are in the sentence: «A babysitter is a trusted person who looks after children while parents are out.» The words while parents are out tell you when a babysitter is needed.
explain: Parents often leave phone numbers and rules for the babysitter. «Parents leave phone numbers and rules so the babysitter knows who to call.» So a babysitter needs to know the rules and who to call if there is an emergency.
explain: The word can also be used informally for something that keeps children busy so adults can rest, like a TV. Ask yourself: is this a person or a thing? The context tells you which meaning the writer means.
fact: A babysitter is a person who looks after children in their home while the parents are out.
fact: Babysitters are often older teenagers or adults, and they are often paid for the job.
fact: A good babysitter knows where the first-aid kit is and how to call for help in an emergency.
fact: «Even married parents need time just for the two of them, so on date night a trusted babysitter comes.»
fact: Informally, «a babysitter» can mean something that keeps children busy, like a TV, so that adults can rest.
exercise: What is a babysitter? | *A person who looks after children in their home while the parents are out | A doctor who visits sick children | A teacher who works at a school | A parent who never goes out in the evening
exercise: «On date night a trusted babysitter comes.» What does trusted mean here? | *Someone the parents can rely on to be safe | Someone who is always late | Someone who never speaks | Someone who is very tired
exercise: Why do parents leave phone numbers and rules for the babysitter? | *So the babysitter knows who to call | So the children can play games all night | Because babysitters cannot read | So the babysitter can pay for the dinner
test: «The TV was a babysitter for the twins while Mum cooked.» What does babysitter mean here? | A person who taught the twins to read | A cook who made dinner for the family | *Something that kept the twins busy so Mum could rest | A doctor who checked the twins
test: Which word means a person who looks after children while parents are out? | gardener | teacher | neighbour | *babysitter
exam: «A babysitter should know where the first-aid kit is.» What is a good babysitter able to do? | Cook a meal for the whole street | *Find the first-aid kit and call for help in an emergency | Sing to the parents at the door | Fly a plane to the shops
